C6  the banked bound rank Cat_{2,2}(l.c) <= 2r (theory_directions sec.B(a))
    r = 10:  bound 2r = 20;  measured rank Cat_22(l.c) = 20,  rank Cat_22(x_0.per_3) = 18
    Both at or below the banked bound; the direction failure is s35's
    proved lemma, not a new phenomenon.  New here: the det side is 36 at
    r >= 8 (full rank at r <= 7), which is what fixes the minor size.

C2  rank Hess(per_3) on {per_3 = 0}, all coordinates nonzero
    all coordinates nonzero                          rank distribution over 40 draws: {9: 40}
    coordinates from [-6,6] (the first run's sampler) rank distribution over 40 draws: {8: 17, 9: 23}
    The dual dimension is the value at a GENERAL point, i.e. the maximum
    of a lower-semicontinuous function: 9, hence dim X^* = 7.  Rank 10
    never occurs, which is the padding identity.

C3  a rank-2 point of a 5-dimensional pencil is an ORDINARY node
    seed   P(s)   grad P(s)   rank Hess P(s)   ordinary node?
       1   0      0                   4        yes
       2   0      0                   4        yes
       3   0      0                   4        yes
       4   0      0                   4        yes
    rank = r-1 = 4 at the singular point is exactly the condition for an
    ordinary node (A_1) of a hypersurface in P^4: the projective Hessian
    always has the point itself in its kernel, so 4 is the maximum.
